# Learner-generated artifacts from running this lab in place — never committed.
# The lab's canonical HCL is hello.tf / bucket.tf (tracked, drift-checked).
# The lock file is generated: verify.sh now runs `tofu init -backend=false` here
# (US-C-GATE). It stays UNCOMMITTED for a teaching reason, not a technical one —
# `tofu init` records all-platform h1: hashes, so a committed lock would work
# fine in CI. Lab 03 teaches `tofu init` CREATING the lock file ("OpenTofu has
# created a lock file .terraform.lock.hcl") and asks the learner what it is for;
# a pre-existing lock turns that into "Reusing previous version ..." and the
# lesson stops reproducing.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
hello.txt
crash.log
crash.*.log
